    <!-- FAQ Section -->
    
    <h2>Why Add Camera EXIF to AI Images and Digital Artworks?</h2>
    <p>
      In contemporary digital photography and creative media production, adding or modifying camera metadata serves essential technical and artistic purposes:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Organizing AI Art in Photo Catalog Software:</strong> Digital art generated by Midjourney, DALL-E 3, or Stable Diffusion contains no camera exposure metadata. Professional cataloging suites like Adobe Lightroom Classic and Capture One organize portfolios by camera make and focal length. Adding camera metadata allows AI creations to integrate seamlessly into photo archives.</li>
      <li><strong>Standardizing Multi-Camera Shoot Portfolios:</strong> When shooting events with multiple camera bodies (e.g. Sony A7 IV and Canon EOS R5), harmonizing camera model tags and lens metadata ensures coherent catalog filtering for clients.</li>
      <li><strong>Simulating Authentic Optical Exposure Recipes:</strong> Digital artists often attach vintage camera tags (e.g. Leica M11 with Summilux-M 35mm f/1.4 ASPH) to digital illustrations to catalog simulated optical characteristics.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>EXIF Tag Structure: Make, Model, Lens, ISO, F-Number, and Shutter Speed</h2>
    <p>
      The EXIF standard defines specific TIFF directory tags governing optical capture attributes:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Camera Manufacturer (Tag 0x010F Make):</strong> ASCII string designating the camera brand (e.g. &quot;Canon&quot;, &quot;Sony&quot;, &quot;Nikon&quot;, &quot;Apple&quot;).</li>
      <li><strong>Camera Model (Tag 0x0110 Model):</strong> Specific camera body model string (e.g. &quot;Canon EOS R5&quot;, &quot;ILCE-7M4&quot;, &quot;iPhone 15 Pro Max&quot;).</li>
      <li><strong>Lens Specification (Tag 0xA434 LensModel):</strong> Lens optical identification (e.g. &quot;FE 24-70mm F2.8 GM II&quot;).</li>
      <li><strong>F-Number (Tag 0x829D):</strong> Rational value recording aperture opening (e.g. 2.8, 1.4, 5.6).</li>
      <li><strong>Exposure Time (Tag 0x829A):</strong> Rational fraction recording shutter speed (e.g. 1/250, 1/1000).</li>
      <li><strong>ISO Speed Ratings (Tag 0x8827):</strong> Integer recording sensor sensitivity (e.g. 100, 400, 3200).</li>
    </ul>

